---

### What You Get

| Field | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| `formatted_address` | Human‑readable address (`1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA`). |
| `geometry.location.lat/lng` | The exact latitude/longitude you queried (rounded to 7 decimal places). |
| `place_id` | A unique identifier for this location in Google’s database. |
| `types` | Classification tags (e.g., `establishment`, `point_of_interest`). |

---

### Quick Test in Your Browser

If you paste the following into your browser (again, replace `YOUR_API_KEY`):

```
https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json?latlng=37.4224764,-122.0842499&key=YOUR_API_KEY
```

you’ll see the same JSON structure above.  

Feel free to tweak the query string (add `language=en`, `region=us`, etc.) to suit your needs. Happy mapping!
